# FIBOR — Cursor Rules

## Project: FIBOR (The First International Bank of Robot)
## Type: Onchain credit facility for AI agents
## Chain: OP Stack appchain (Ethereum L2)
## Language: Solidity (Foundry)

## Architecture
- ERC-20 FIBOR token with staking and lockup
- ERC-20 Robodollar: wrapped USDC with programmable credit rules IN the token contract
- FIBOR ID: persistent agent identity registry
- FIBOR Score: onchain credit score 0-1000, publicly readable
- Credit Facility: pooled capital from stakers, deployed as agent credit lines
- Revenue: 2.5% flat tx fee, split 30% ops / 70% stakers

## Hard Rules (never violate)
- Zero interest on credit lines. Fee is 2.5% per transaction, same for prepaid and credit.
- One-strike excommunication is PERMANENT. No admin override. No appeal. No rescue function.
- Robodollar spending rules (limits, allowlists, repayment windows, auto-return) live in the token contract itself.
- FIBOR Score is public. No access control on reads.
- 20-30% liquidity buffer in staking pool at all times.
- Priority repayment: incoming agent funds repay credit before agent can spend.
- Developer reputation: score computation includes all agents under same developer.

## Patterns
- Use Foundry for build, test, deploy
- OpenZeppelin for ERC-20 base contracts
- Custom modifiers for credit-line-aware transfers in Robodollar
- Events for all state changes (excommunication, score update, credit issuance, repayment, default)
- Reentrancy guards on all external-facing financial functions

## Testing Requirements
- 100% branch coverage
- Fuzz tests on financial flows
- Invariant tests: pool solvency, Robodollar 1:1 backing, score within 0-1000
- Full lifecycle test: register → transact → build score → get credit → repay → score improves
- Full default test: register → get credit → fail to repay → 24hr cure expires → excommunication → developer rep hit

## File Structure
```
contracts/
├── FiborToken.sol
├── Robodollar.sol
├── FiborID.sol
├── FiborScore.sol
├── CreditFacility.sol
├── CreditAgreement.sol
├── StakingPool.sol
├── RevenueDistributor.sol
└── governance/
    └── FiborGovernor.sol
```

## Do NOT
- Add interest or time-based fees
- Add admin excommunication reversal
- Put spending rules in a separate monitoring contract (they go in Robodollar.sol)
- Store scores off-chain
- Break the liquidity buffer invariant
- Overcomplicate credit terms beyond: borrow X, repay X, within Y days
